                note: "Strapping pin (MTDI), internal pull-down: HIGH at reset sets VDD_SDIO (flash supply) to 1.8 V, so a 3.3 V flash can fail to flash or boot. Also JTAG TDI after reset: a connected JTAG adapter overrides the pull-down. With 3.3 V flash keep it low at reset or burn espefuse set-flash-voltage 3.3V (permanent) so it is ignored. ADC2: unusable while Wi-Fi is on. Erratum GPIO-3.14: once one pad in GPIO0-31 (or in GPIO32-39) has an edge interrupt, no other interrupt may be used in that group, as edges can be missed while the group\'s shared status register is accessed. The generated IRQ code always waits for edges and esp-hal has no workaround: arm at most one IRQ pad in GPIO0-27 and one in GPIO32-39.",
