                note: "Strapping pin, internal pull-down: it must be LOW or floating at reset for a LOW GPIO0 to start the serial bootloader; with GPIO0 high its level is ignored. A pull-up here at reset (e.g. an SD card\'s DAT0 pull-up) blocks download mode. ADC2: unusable while Wi-Fi is on (esp-hal also locks it while Bluetooth runs). Erratum GPIO-3.14: once one pad in GPIO0-31 (or in GPIO32-39) has an edge interrupt, no other interrupt may be used in that group, as edges can be missed while the group\'s shared status register is accessed. The generated IRQ code always waits for edges and esp-hal has no workaround: arm at most one IRQ pad in GPIO0-27 and one in GPIO32-39.",
