                note: "Strapping pin, internal pull-up (about 45k): LOW at reset, with GPIO2 low, starts the ROM serial bootloader instead of the flash program - this is where a BOOT button and esptool\'s DTR auto-reset line connect. Keep large capacitors and power-up pull-downs off it. ADC2: unusable while Wi-Fi is on (esp-hal also locks it while Bluetooth runs). Erratum GPIO-3.14: once one pad in GPIO0-31 (or in GPIO32-39) has an edge interrupt, no other interrupt may be used in that group, as edges can be missed while the group\'s shared status register is accessed. The generated IRQ code always waits for edges and esp-hal has no workaround: arm at most one IRQ pad in GPIO0-27 and one in GPIO32-39.",
